{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1040", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "\"\n**MATTHIAS ALGIERS**\n\n**PROFILE**\n\nDYNAMIC INDUSTRIAL ENGINEER WITH A PROVEN TRACK RECORD IN PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND PROCESS IMPROVEMENT.\n\n**KEY SKILLS**\n\n- **LEADERSHIP:** EXCELLED IN LEADING CROSS-FUNCTIONAL TEAMS TO ACHIEVE PROJECT GOALS.\n- **PROBLEM-SOLVING:** EFFECTIVE IN IDENTIFYING AND RESOLVING OPERATIONAL CHALLENGES.\n- **COMMUNICATION:** CLEAR AND CONCISE COMMUNICATION SKILLS TO ENSURE EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION.\n- **TECHNICAL EXPERTISE:** WELL-VERSED IN INDUSTRIAL ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES AND SOFTWARE (SIMULATION, CAD).\n- **QUALITY ASSURANCE:** STRONG FOCUS ON QUALITY CONTROL AND PROCESS OPTIMIZATION.\n\n**EXPERIENCE**\n\n**SENIOR INDUSTRIAL ENGINEER**\nXYZ CORPORATION, ANNE ARUNDEL COUNTY, MD\n2018 - PRESENT\n- **IMPLEMENTED LEAN MANUFACTURING PRACTICES** TO REDUCE WASTE AND INCREASE PRODUCTIVITY BY 20%.\n- **LED THE DESIGN AND IMPLEMENTATION** OF A NEW PRODUCTION LINE, RESULTING IN A 15% INCREASE IN THROUGHPUT.\n- **MANAGED MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAMS** TO OVERCOME SUPPLY CHAIN DISRUPTIONS AND MEET DEADLINES.\n- **DEVELOPED SIMULATION MODELS** TO ANALYZE PROCESS EFFICIENCY AND IDENTIFY AREAS FOR IMPROVEMENT.\n\n**JUNIOR INDUSTRIAL ENGINEER**\nABC INDUSTRIES, BALTIMORE, MD\n2015 - 2018\n- **COLLABORATED WITH OPERATIONS AND QUALITY ASSURANCE TEAMS** TO IMPROVE PRODUCT QUALITY AND REDUCE DEFECTS BY 10%.\n- **CONDUCTED PROCESS FLOW ANALYSES** TO IDENTIFY AND ELIMINATE NON-VALUE-ADDING ACTIVITIES.\n- **DEVELOPED TRAINING MATERIALS** FOR NEW EMPLOYEES TO ENSURE CONSISTENT PROCESS ADHERENCE.\n\n**EDUCATION**\n\nM.S. IN INDUSTRIAL ENGINEERING\nUNIVERSITY OF MARYLAND, COLLEGE PARK\n2015 - 2018\nB.S. IN INDUSTRIAL ENGINEERING\nUNIVERSITY OF MARYLAND, COLLEGE PARK\n2011 - 2015\n\n**CERTIFICATIONS**\n\n- **LEAN SIX SIGMA BLACK BELT**\n- **PROJECT MANAGEMENT PROFESSIONAL (PMP)**\n\n\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.02462838